WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:02.309
Your support of Bitcoin puts you

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.199
in the same category as

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.699
the framers of the Constitution.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:06.599
Bitcoin is special.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:07.129
Bitcoin

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:08.099
is the future.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.169
Bitcoin will undermine their ability

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:11.629
to control us.

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:13.099
It has all the trappings of a

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:13.169
religion.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:14.909
Those who are not getting into

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.859
Bitcoin now, it's because their DNA

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.839
was not meant to survive.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:20.069
FTX is the safest and easiest way to

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:20.939
buy and sell crypto.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.619
Sam Bankman-Fried is in federal

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:24.179
court right now for his arraignment.

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.189
The collapse of FTX gave the

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:27.899
Biden admin a perceived moral

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.879
license to go after crypto

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:30.899
in this aggressive way.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.459
And the governments aren't exactly

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.049
going to let us walk in the front

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.059
door with this new open source money

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.109
called Bitcoin.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:38.609
Everything you're seeing now we've

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.409
seen before, there's nothing new.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:41.970
It is just typical Bitcoin.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.229
15 years after Satoshi Nakamoto

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.029
dropped a nine page white paper on

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.889
an obscure email list sketching out

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:52.049
an idea for a new peer-to-peer

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:53.969
digital currency, Bitcoin has become

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:55.889
a global phenomenon, and nowhere is

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:58.229
its pomp and promise more on display

00:00:58.230 --> 00:00:59.609
than at the blockbuster annual

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:01.289
conference put on by Bitcoin

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.089
Magazine here in Miami Beach.

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:04.738
But it's also had a disappointing

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:05.639
couple of years.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.169
Bitcoin was supposed to be an

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:09.059
inflation hedge, but after the Fed

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:10.559
fired up its money printer during

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:12.839
the pandemic, the dollar lost value

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.729
and Bitcoin went in the same

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:16.619
direction. Bitcoin was supposed to

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.569
be a way to transfer money from one

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:20.309
party to another without going

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.199
through a financial institution, to

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.099
quote Satoshi.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.959
But 15 years later, a lot of

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:26.274
users are still trusting regulated

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.429
financial institutions to manage

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:30.209
their holdings.

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.039
Bitcoin was supposed to be above

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.019
politics, but the community around

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.579
it has seen bitter infighting.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:37.079
Just saying that's how not how you

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:38.309
use Bitcoin, though.

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:39.539
That's not how you use it.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:40.559
You should use Bitcoin in this

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:41.429
particular way.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:42.899
And some worry that Bitcoiners

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:45.149
intolerance of dissenting ideas

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:47.009
has turned it into something akin to

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:48.419
a religion or a cult.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.279
And yet the bitcoiners we talked to

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:51.869
in Miami seemed convinced that its

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:54.209
value proposition as a decentralized

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:55.979
money that governments can't censor

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:58.079
or destroy is as strong as ever.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.969
Are Bitcoin's troubles a sign

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.559
that the project is failing, or just

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.179
the inevitable bumps on an upward

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.339
trajectory which will one day result

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.559
in monetary freedom for the entire

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.560
world?

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:12.419
Attendance here at one of the

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:14.039
largest Bitcoin conferences in the

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.089
world

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.188
is down by more than half amid this

00:02:17.189 --> 00:02:18.129
so-called crypto winter.

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:19.199
I think if you were to compare like

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.999
last year's conference to this

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:21.599
year's one,

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.789
Very noticeable dramatic difference.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:26.069
I'm not a fan of the

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:28.499
mania bull run phases

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:30.329
because of the type of people

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:31.679
that it attracts.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:33.479
You might call them the tourists or

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.549
the larpers or in many cases

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:36.539
the scammers.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.549
There is a big chunk of crypto

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:39.809
that needs to burn on a raging

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:40.799
funeral pyre.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.839
There were criminals,

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.849
scammers, grifters, overleveraged

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.289
business models that should never

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:48.399
have been implemented.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.639
FTX has arrived in 305.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:51.429
So I just got one question.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:52.430
You in, Miami?

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:57.889
Just a few miles away from this

00:02:57.890 --> 00:02:59.479
year's conference is the Miami

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:01.669
Heat's home court, formerly called

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:04.009
FTX Arena after the crypto platform

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:05.989
paid $135 million

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:08.119
for the naming rights back in 2021.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.309
In January, when FTX collapsed

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:12.139
into bankruptcy and its founder, Sam

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:13.519
Bankman-Fried, was arrested for

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.379
alleged fraud, the signage was

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.419
removed. Bitcoiners believe that any

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:19.549
cryptocurrency other than Satoshi's

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:21.559
original creation should be referred

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:23.659
to as a shitcoin and that the crypto

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:25.639
industry is a cargo cult run

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.469
by scammers who have the mainstream

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:29.389
media and much of Silicon Valley

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:31.519
fooled. Exhibit A, Sam

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:32.599
Bankman-Fried.

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:33.769
He's a criminal. He should go to

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:35.599
jail. People who conflate what they

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:36.499
did with Bitcoin have got it

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:37.309
entirely wrong.

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:38.449
The way I like to describe the

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:41.359
crypto industry and blockchain

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.009
is it's an arbitrage on the trend.

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:44.299
It's sad and it's discussing.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:45.229
It's got to stop.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:47.209
Bitcoiners also see the FTX

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:48.769
collapse as a reminder that you

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:50.779
can't trust bankers or tech founder

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:53.089
media darlings like Bankman-Fried

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:54.529
to take care of your savings,

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:55.969
whether they're outright scammers or

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:58.219
not. Banks must be trusted to hold

00:03:58.220 --> 00:03:59.449
our money and transfer it

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:01.339
electronically, but they lend it

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.109
out in waves of credit bubbles with

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:04.909
barely a fraction in reserve,

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:06.739
Satoshi wrote in 2009.

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:08.599
The message is, trust nobody

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.099
and become your own bank, which

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:11.539
Bitcoin makes possible.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:12.799
I think it just shows that, like

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:14.539
these large centralized institutions

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:15.609
are always going to be at risk.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:17.809
So the ethos of Bitcoin is not about

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:19.129
putting all of your money into a

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:21.229
giant centralized custodian.

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:22.459
So like, none of that would have

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:24.469
happened in TradFi because everyone

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:25.609
would have been bolstered, everyone

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:26.479
would have been bailed out.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.369
But in crypto, the bad actors were

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.259
allowed to implode publicly and

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:31.189
people got hurt.

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:33.349
But that overall is just the

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:35.089
immune system for crypto showing

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:35.539
itself.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:37.399
Another reason to be your own bank

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.259
is to avoid financial censorship

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:40.909
so that everyone from third world

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:42.859
dictators to DC regulators

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:44.419
is prevented from telling you how

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:46.009
you should spend your money.

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:47.839
The fall of FTX precipitated

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.489
a crackdown in Washington that was

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:51.319
meant to send a very strong

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:53.299
anti-crypto message, in the words

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:55.039
of former Congressman Barney Frank.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:57.379
We don't need more digital currency.

00:04:57.380 --> 00:04:58.969
We already have digital currency.

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:00.139
It's called the US Dollar.

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:02.269
FTX certainly gave them political

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:03.319
cover to do this.

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:05.299
Then they opened up the toolkit and

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.279
they went to their favorite

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.229
tool, which is politicizing

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:10.729
the instruments of finance.

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:12.589
Nick Carter is a writer and crypto

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:14.149
investor who coined the phrase

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:16.069
Operation Choke Point 2.0,

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:18.199
a reference to the Obama era policy

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.879
of bullying banks into denying

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:21.499
accounts to payday lenders,

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:23.509
pornographers, firearms dealers,

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:25.249
strippers, and other fully legal

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:26.869
industries that regulators would

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:27.979
rather see disappear.

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:29.989
So again, a perfectly legal

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:31.819
industry in the US that's

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:33.649
being targeted through the

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:35.269
bank regulatory apparatus.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:37.129
It really kicked off this

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:38.239
year in January.

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:39.979
It involved virtually every

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:42.139
financial regulatory agency,

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:43.939
in particular the bank regulators.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:46.009
And the objective was to stymie the

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:47.899
legal crypto industry in the US,

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:50.269
not through any lawful mechanism,

00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:52.909
but through insinuations,

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:54.019
through threats.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.999
Operation Choke Point 1.0 was

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.229
carried out by the Consumer

00:05:57.230 --> 00:05:58.969
Financial Protection Bureau, which

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:00.529
was the brainchild of Elizabeth

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:02.269
Warren, and now she's become the

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:04.549
Senate's most vocal Bitcoin critic.

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:06.379
If I buy Bitcoin, am I buying a

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:08.329
share of stock or am

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:10.519
I buying a pork belly?

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:12.349
Or are you buying air?

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:14.449
Rogue nations, oligarchs, drug

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:16.159
lords and human traffickers are

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:18.049
using digital assets to launder

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:20.269
billions in stolen funds,

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:22.279
evade sanctions, and finance

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:24.139
terrorism, Warren said last

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:25.669
year when promoting a bill that

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:27.169
would extend the state's power to

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:28.819
surveil people's finances.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:31.069
Crypto is helping fund the fentanyl

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:33.019
trade, and we have the power

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:33.889
to shut that down.

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:35.629
If I were Elizabeth Warren, what

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:36.679
would you say to me?

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:38.239
First of all, I'd shake your hand.

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:39.319
I would say, hi, it's really good to

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:40.639
meet you.

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:42.769
I would also say you are

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:44.989
purposely misinformed about crypto.

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:46.219
She doesn't have Bitcoin.

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:47.689
She doesn't understand energy.

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:49.039
She's part of the elite.

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:50.989
She's part of the corrupt political

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:52.189
structure in the U.S.

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:53.269
and she's anti-human.

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:54.109
She's anti-freedom.

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:55.819
I've been trying to clean up this

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:56.820
industry

00:06:57.950 --> 00:06:59.869
for a while because I firmly

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:01.819
believe that there are

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.469
affronts to private property rights.

00:07:03.470 --> 00:07:05.359
Caitlin Long, who spent 22 years

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.429
in corporate finance, is the founder

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:09.019
of Custodial, which she hopes will

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:11.149
become America's first Bitcoin bank.

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:12.919
It's designed to be the antithesis

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:14.749
of the company run by Bankman-Fried,

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:16.969
whom Long clashed with on stage

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:18.829
at the same Bitcoin conference back

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:20.149
in 2021.

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:22.189
Satoshi gave us money

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:23.839
that isn't debt.

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:25.669
I like to use the phrase, a fool

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:27.229
and their leveraged Bitcoin are soon

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:28.039
parted.

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:29.659
Sam, do you agree?

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:30.550
Not with a lot of it.

00:07:30.551 --> 00:07:31.551
I

00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:34.669
guess that's not shocking.

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:36.529
FTX allegedly squandered its

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:37.699
customers holdings.

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:39.619
Custodia, by contrast, plans

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:41.179
to go much further than even a

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:43.129
regulated retail bank by keeping

00:07:43.130 --> 00:07:45.109
108% of its customers

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:46.939
cash in Bitcoin on hand at

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:47.809
all times.

00:07:47.810 --> 00:07:49.249
Thus, it won't have any need for

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:51.289
federal deposit insurance.

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:52.549
Look, you can take the position

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:53.449
leverage is bad.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:54.939
It's not a crazy thing to think.

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:56.979
However, I think you probably also

00:07:56.980 --> 00:07:58.869
have to be willing

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:00.759
to sacrifice more than most people

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:03.039
realize in order to get there.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:04.779
I think you have had to sacrifice

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:06.159
the majority of the growth that the

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:07.269
industry has had to date.

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:08.619
And he and I were arguing over

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:09.939
whether leverage was good.

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:12.189
Leverage is never good

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:14.409
in crypto, period.

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:16.449
Anything that is circulation credit

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:18.459
that goes above one times

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:19.509
leverage, right?

00:08:19.510 --> 00:08:21.339
That is creating claims

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:23.259
to the underlying out of thin

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:24.879
air. It is fractional reserve

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:27.129
banking and we are fundamentally

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:29.079
committed to not doing that.

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:30.699
All of those crypto lenders I knew

00:08:30.700 --> 00:08:32.199
were going to fail. Why?

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:33.908
Because there's a finite number of

00:08:33.909 --> 00:08:34.899
bitcoin.

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:35.979
All you're doing is creating

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:37.928
fractional reserve Bitcoin

00:08:37.929 --> 00:08:39.788
and that's all going to come

00:08:39.789 --> 00:08:42.158
back to haunt you when inevitably

00:08:42.159 --> 00:08:42.969
there's going to be a price

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:44.349
correction and everybody wants the

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:45.369
real thing.

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:47.349
Yet the Federal Reserve rejected

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:49.539
Custodia's application to become

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:50.979
a member of its network on the

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:52.899
grounds that its, quote,

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:54.969
crypto activities are highly likely

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:56.769
to be inconsistent with safe and

00:08:56.770 --> 00:08:58.449
sound banking practices.

00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:00.399
So the crypto industry was proposing

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.259
a solution to the inherent

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:04.149
instability of the banking sector,

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:06.069
and yet that solution was denied

00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:07.539
because the Federal Reserve didn't

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:09.669
want to give a crypto focused

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:11.739
bank access to the payment system.

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:12.939
It's extremely perverse.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:14.919
Long is suing the Federal Reserve

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:16.959
to force it to reconsider, but part

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:18.669
of Satoshi's vision was to create a

00:09:18.670 --> 00:09:20.559
system in which regulatory approval

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:21.729
wasn't necessary.

00:09:21.730 --> 00:09:23.199
Bitcoin is the first digital

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.689
currency you can hold yourself.

00:09:25.690 --> 00:09:27.669
So why do we need to trust a third

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:29.169
party middleman at all?

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:30.429
You read the whitepaper.

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:32.799
You read what Satoshi said.

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:35.019
Trusted third parties are security

00:09:35.020 --> 00:09:35.799
holes.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:37.869
Jameson Lopp is a Bitcoin developer

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:39.789
and the co-founder of Casa, which

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:40.769
helps its customers safely

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:43.059
self-custody the secret passwords

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:44.919
or keys necessary to spend their

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:46.839
Bitcoin. If you lose them, the money

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:47.769
is as good as gone.

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:48.879
But if you're not holding them

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:51.069
yourself, are they really yours?

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:52.689
The Bitcoin writer and evangelist

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:54.699
Andreas Antonopoulos coined

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:56.379
a popular saying in the space.

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:58.149
Your keys, your bitcoin.

00:09:58.150 --> 00:09:59.827
Not your keys, not your bitcoin.

00:09:59.828 --> 00:10:01.749
Your keys, your

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:03.879
bitcoin. Not your keys, not

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:04.959
your bitcoin.

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:06.189
Most people don't want to be their

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:07.839
own bank. But what we're really

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:10.419
saying is like, if you want to have

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:12.579
a level of bank

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:14.499
security, if you want to be able to

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:16.419
operate in such a way that

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:18.009
you don't have to ask permission

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:20.049
from a third party, then

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:21.219
you do have to take on some

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:22.239
responsibility.

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:24.159
Self-custody especially appeals to

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:25.959
Bitcoiners worried about Operation

00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:27.849
Choke Point 2.0 and the plight of

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:29.859
the Canadian truckers who occupied

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:31.599
Ottawa last year to protest a

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:33.519
cross-border COVID vaccine mandate.

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:35.109
Prime Minister Justin Trudeau

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:36.699
responded to the demonstrators by

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:38.889
using emergency powers to force

00:10:38.890 --> 00:10:40.809
financial institutions to freeze

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:42.639
all funds set to support the

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:43.419
cause.

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:44.441
These illegal

00:10:44.442 --> 00:10:46.659
blockades and occupations received

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:48.939
disturbing amounts of foreign

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:49.659
funding.

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:51.729
So a group of activists used Bitcoin

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:53.559
as it was meant to be used, getting

00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:55.749
about $630,000

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:56.949
worth to the truckers.

00:10:56.950 --> 00:10:58.659
Since the funds didn't go through

00:10:58.660 --> 00:11:00.309
the traditional banking system, they

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:01.419
were hard to stop.

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:03.219
An activist filmed himself handing

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:05.079
out seed phrases, or the code words

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:06.789
used to access self-custodied

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:08.739
Bitcoin. This grassroots solution

00:11:08.740 --> 00:11:10.569
was imperfect, laborious, and

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:11.709
in need of improvement.

00:11:11.710 --> 00:11:13.329
But in the end it worked.

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:15.249
A world where most people hold their

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:16.959
own Bitcoin keys would be a world

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:18.609
far more resistant to financial

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:19.959
censorship and surveillance.

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:21.369
But is it really possible?

00:11:21.370 --> 00:11:22.689
It's definitely a breach of a

00:11:22.690 --> 00:11:24.609
person's privacy,

00:11:24.610 --> 00:11:25.809
freezing their bank accounts,

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:27.669
especially if they've committed no

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:28.749
real crimes.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:30.579
Do you think there's ever a future

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:32.229
where we can get grandmas to

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:33.249
self-custody?

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:34.539
Well, it's definitely possible.

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.399
And I can tell you from experience,

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:38.349
we have plenty of people in

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:40.449
their eighties who are clients

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:41.289
of Casa.

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:42.699
The answer lies somewhere in the

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:44.409
middle. I think we will have a

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:46.659
diverse ecosystem and range

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:48.669
of custody and

00:11:48.670 --> 00:11:50.679
it doesn't actually necessarily

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:52.599
need to be a binary thing.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:54.669
It doesn't have to be just trusted

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:57.399
third party or just self-custody.

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:59.379
What really worries me is

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:01.419
if too much of the Bitcoin goes into

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:03.159
too few hands, especially if they're

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:05.559
like regulated companies

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:06.879
that can be easily targeted by

00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:09.009
nation states, that is when

00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:10.909
Bitcoin itself,

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:13.419
you know, as a network

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:15.399
becomes a bit

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:17.349
more prone to nation

00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:18.399
state actions.

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:20.229
And that for many at this conference

00:12:20.230 --> 00:12:22.359
is the entire point of Bitcoin.

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:23.829
Effective resistance against

00:12:23.830 --> 00:12:25.419
authoritarian government action.

00:12:26.650 --> 00:12:28.809
As most of you know, that trucker

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:31.749
strike was a peaceful demonstration

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:33.879
of people who are demanding rights

00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:35.889
that are sacred and are

00:12:35.890 --> 00:12:37.599
taken for granted for every

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:38.600
American.

00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:40.899
Walking around the conference, all

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:42.399
of the elements of the Bitcoiners

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:44.349
creed were on full display, which

00:12:44.350 --> 00:12:46.149
Nick Carter says has turned into a

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:47.979
religion. It has its own heroes,

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:50.229
icons, doctrines, saints,

00:12:50.230 --> 00:12:51.279
and heretics.

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:53.049
On one hand, having a devoted

00:12:53.050 --> 00:12:54.519
following that won't abandon a

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:56.269
project through the rough patches is

00:12:56.270 --> 00:12:57.461
a key to long term success.

00:12:57.462 --> 00:12:59.869
On the other, fanaticism

00:12:59.870 --> 00:13:01.639
leads to poor decision making and

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:03.469
can drive away vital allies.

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:04.669
Certainly not the only secular

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:07.339
religion out there, but it's a

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:08.779
particularly pernicious breed.

00:13:08.780 --> 00:13:10.459
Nick Carter was in Miami this year

00:13:10.460 --> 00:13:11.899
during the conference, but says he

00:13:11.900 --> 00:13:13.579
didn't attend any of the sessions

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:15.079
because of safety concerns.

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:16.789
Much of the community turned on him

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:17.869
when it was revealed that his

00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:19.339
investment fund had a stake in

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:20.809
cryptocurrencies other than just

00:13:20.810 --> 00:13:22.819
Bitcoin. So he penned a eulogy

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:24.649
for Bitcoin maximalism declaring

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:26.299
that there's an awful sickness

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:27.499
pervading the space.

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:29.359
I have been a full time Bitcoiner

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:31.219
for ten years and I've dedicated my

00:13:31.220 --> 00:13:33.169
professional and personal

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:34.977
efforts to the sector tirelessly

00:13:34.978 --> 00:13:36.319
that whole time.

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:37.789
And yet, because I'm more of a

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:39.769
Bitcoin moderate a lot of the

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:41.779
hard liner Bitcoiners don't like me,

00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:43.459
but I think what we need to realize

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:45.559
is our enemy

00:13:45.560 --> 00:13:47.509
is not inward.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:49.369
We shouldn't be doing this circular

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:50.509
firing squad thing.

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:51.739
Something all Bitcoiners have been

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:53.059
saying for years is there's a big

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:54.529
difference between Bitcoin and

00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:56.329
crypto, a distinction that now even

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:57.709
the head of the S.E.C., Gary

00:13:57.710 --> 00:13:59.389
Gensler, made when talking about

00:13:59.390 --> 00:14:00.559
crypto regulation.

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:02.059
Speaking Monday on CNBC,

00:14:02.060 --> 00:14:02.868
Gensler said

00:14:02.869 --> 00:14:04.009
that Bitcoin is the only

00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:05.899
cryptocurrency that he is prepared

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:07.609
to label publicly as a commodity.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:09.859
There has been a decent amount

00:14:09.860 --> 00:14:12.529
from Bitcoiners, some that I respect

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:14.239
that have essentially been cheering

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:16.129
on government attacking people.

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:18.109
The end game is attacking Bitcoin.

00:14:18.110 --> 00:14:20.269
There's an expression in crypto.

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:22.369
Not your keys, not

00:14:22.370 --> 00:14:23.089
your

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:24.079
crypto. Bitcoiners should be trying

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:26.359
to win in the free market and

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:28.189
organize Bitcoin such that

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:30.379
it is the most compelling

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:32.479
blockchain, the most credible

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:35.089
one, the most decentralized.

00:14:35.090 --> 00:14:36.559
They should not be trying to utilize

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:38.029
the instruments of state power to

00:14:38.030 --> 00:14:40.279
suppress their perceived

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:41.779
adversaries.

00:14:41.780 --> 00:14:43.669
Bitcoin has

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:44.479
its own merits.

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:46.489
It stands on its own two feet.

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:48.469
We don't need financial regulators

00:14:48.470 --> 00:14:49.999
to try and pick and choose which

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:50.689
winners there are.

00:14:50.690 --> 00:14:52.489
Jameson Lopp has also been on the

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:54.179
receiving end of Bitcoin maximalist

00:14:54.180 --> 00:14:56.029
rage after his company, Casa,

00:14:56.030 --> 00:14:57.769
made the business decision to expand

00:14:57.770 --> 00:14:59.419
its service to help Ethereum owners

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:00.979
self-custody their holdings.

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:02.989
In 2019, a teenager called

00:15:02.990 --> 00:15:05.119
in a SWAT raid on his home because,

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:06.649
according to Lopp, the kid didn't

00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:07.939
like his opinion about how the

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:09.499
Bitcoin protocol should function.

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:11.419
In response, Lopp shared a video of

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:13.249
himself firing an AR-15

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:14.659
on Twitter. Then he took

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:16.639
extraordinary steps to make himself

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:18.285
impossible to track down in

00:15:18.286 --> 00:15:19.519
meatspace, which was later written

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:20.689
up by the New York Times.

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:22.879
It's a result of social media.

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:25.249
You can instantly

00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:27.289
go from being essentially

00:15:27.290 --> 00:15:29.269
a nobody with

00:15:29.270 --> 00:15:31.189
no one paying attention to you,

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:33.889
to being someone who has

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:35.749
attracted the ire of millions of

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:37.309
people in a matter of moment.

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:39.379
It's similar to sort of political

00:15:39.380 --> 00:15:42.269
theater and phenomenon where

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:43.699
you build up your narratives, you

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:45.169
build your audience and you're

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:47.659
following in your community and

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:49.939
in one of the ways that you

00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:51.889
create a more cohesive

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:53.869
audience is by having enemies

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:55.129
that you attack in certain

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:56.599
ideological ways.

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:58.489
And so basically that same thing

00:15:58.490 --> 00:16:00.199
has unfolded within Bitcoin.

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:01.639
Most of the religious imagery

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:02.929
present at the conference was

00:16:02.930 --> 00:16:04.219
shrouded in irony.

00:16:04.220 --> 00:16:06.259
But as with so much of digital life,

00:16:06.260 --> 00:16:07.909
it was hard to tell where the joke

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:08.359
ended.

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:09.679
I don't believe that there's any

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:11.599
moral status in your

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:13.429
portfolio, and there is

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:15.019
a faction within Bitcoin that

00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:17.119
believes that the only moral

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:19.679
asset to hold is Bitcoin itself,

00:16:19.680 --> 00:16:21.289
nothing else. Bitcoin religion is

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:22.759
not a universalizing one.

00:16:22.760 --> 00:16:24.979
It actually just concentrates

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:26.689
the membership and they become

00:16:26.690 --> 00:16:28.279
increasingly radical and

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:30.769
disconnected from the real world.

00:16:30.770 --> 00:16:32.839
So if they want to succeed,

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:34.759
they need to find a way to

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:36.799
grow the membership of the Bitcoin

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:38.629
space rather than

00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:40.159
impose all these additional

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:41.449
requirements in terms of what it

00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:42.679
means to be in Bitcoiner.

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:44.689
As the quasi religious fervor around

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:46.609
Bitcoin has grown, so too

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:48.079
has the potential for a Bitcoin

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:49.879
voting block. Ronald Reagan once

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:51.709
courted the religious right, but in

00:16:51.710 --> 00:16:53.839
2023, a parade of once

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:55.489
and future presidential contenders

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:57.199
made the trek down to Miami to

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:58.639
pander to the Bitcoiners.

00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:00.409
Former Congresswoman Tulsi Gabbard

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:00.889
showed up.

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:02.989
Once we give up our economic

00:17:02.990 --> 00:17:05.179
autonomy, we give up

00:17:05.180 --> 00:17:06.169
our freedom.

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:07.818
Along with longshot presidential

00:17:07.819 --> 00:17:09.348
candidate Vivek Ramaswamy.

00:17:09.349 --> 00:17:11.328
Freedom of speech and freedom

00:17:11.329 --> 00:17:13.368
of money are two sides

00:17:13.369 --> 00:17:14.779
of the same coin.

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:16.699
Perhaps nobody better captured the

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:17.989
mood, though, than, Democratic

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:19.578
presidential candidate Robert F.

00:17:19.579 --> 00:17:21.529
Kennedy Jr, who in his keynote

00:17:21.530 --> 00:17:23.269
speech repeated the anti-elite

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:25.098
populist messaging that is central

00:17:25.099 --> 00:17:26.269
to the Bitcoin creed.

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:27.270
Control over the public starts

00:17:28.820 --> 00:17:30.799
perhaps as a means,

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:32.689
but it always becomes

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:34.699
an end through exercising

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:37.009
perfect control over society.

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:39.049
Bitcoin is a bulwark

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:41.059
against precisely

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:42.439
this kind of government and

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:45.319
corporate expansion and intrusion.

00:17:45.320 --> 00:17:46.309
Like Robert Kennedy, basically what

00:17:46.310 --> 00:17:47.209
he's saying with that was like

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:49.609
government is not your friend.

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:51.079
An art gallery at the conference

00:17:51.080 --> 00:17:52.669
displayed work demonizing Bill

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:54.529
Gates, Anthony Fauci, and the World

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:56.419
Economic Forum's Klaus Schwab.

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:58.459
What do you think about Klaus Schwab?

00:17:58.460 --> 00:17:59.449
Truthfully, I don't think it's

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:01.389
messed up anywhere near enough.

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:02.569
You know, there are certainly a lot

00:18:02.570 --> 00:18:05.569
of people who get turned off by

00:18:05.570 --> 00:18:07.669
some of the vitriol,

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:10.009
whereas other people get interested

00:18:10.010 --> 00:18:10.939
and sucked into it.

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:12.919
But if anything, I think it

00:18:12.920 --> 00:18:14.899
may be overblown that the vast

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:17.719
majority of people who use Bitcoin

00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:19.849
don't know about any of that.

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:22.099
They just see Bitcoin as a thing

00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:23.329
that they're using.

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.579
It's not something

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:27.049
that they have adopted from a

00:18:27.050 --> 00:18:28.159
cultural standpoint.

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:29.539
It's just a tool that they have

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:31.489
adopted because of the properties

00:18:31.490 --> 00:18:32.490
of Bitcoin.

00:18:37.370 --> 00:18:38.370
What's the purpose of Bitcoin?

00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:41.827
To not be with the government.

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:45.849
We should just be focusing on, you

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:47.619
know, what our Bitcoin strengths,

00:18:47.620 --> 00:18:48.969
which is like peer to peer
transactions,

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:50.829
non-KYC transactions and that's

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:52.029
what I'm interested in.

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:53.015
What is Bitcoin?

00:18:53.016 --> 00:18:54.009
To me it's money.

00:18:54.010 --> 00:18:56.139
In the original whitepaper, Satoshi

00:18:56.140 --> 00:18:58.089
described Bitcoin as a peer to peer

00:18:58.090 --> 00:18:59.589
electronic cash system.

00:18:59.590 --> 00:19:01.449
15 years later, it still isn't

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:03.729
widely used as a medium of exchange.

00:19:03.730 --> 00:19:05.229
At first its limitations were

00:19:05.230 --> 00:19:07.179
technical. The network can't process

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:09.279
more than about 7 to 10 transactions

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:10.059
per second.

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:11.529
But a decentralized payment

00:19:11.530 --> 00:19:12.819
technology called the Lightning

00:19:12.820 --> 00:19:15.069
Network is endlessly scalable

00:19:15.070 --> 00:19:16.509
and has made paying for a cup of

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:18.729
coffee with Bitcoin fairly seamless,

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:20.079
though not a lot of people are doing

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:20.439
it yet.

00:19:20.440 --> 00:19:22.209
I have 100% conviction.

00:19:22.210 --> 00:19:23.949
I mean, there's there's zero doubt.

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:25.779
It's just a question of, you

00:19:25.780 --> 00:19:28.629
know, at what pace global adoption

00:19:28.630 --> 00:19:29.679
will take place. Chris Hunter

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:31.509
founded Bitcoin Beach Wallet, a

00:19:31.510 --> 00:19:32.949
lightning based payment software

00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:34.839
that launched in El Salvador, whose

00:19:34.840 --> 00:19:36.789
president, Nayib Bukele, is

00:19:36.790 --> 00:19:38.289
another politician who has

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:40.089
capitalized on his association with

00:19:40.090 --> 00:19:41.169
the Bitcoin community.

00:19:41.170 --> 00:19:43.239
He announced at the 2021 conference

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:45.009
that El Salvador would be first in

00:19:45.010 --> 00:19:47.109
the world to adopt Bitcoin as legal

00:19:47.110 --> 00:19:48.098
currency.

00:19:48.099 --> 00:19:49.599
It was 90 days from the announcement

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:51.489
here in Miami two years ago when

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:52.599
they were going to make Bitcoin

00:19:52.600 --> 00:19:53.589
legal tender.

00:19:53.590 --> 00:19:55.479
Only 90 days later, on September 7,

00:19:55.480 --> 00:19:57.399
2021, did they actually

00:19:57.400 --> 00:19:59.229
launch the implementation with

00:19:59.230 --> 00:20:00.639
their Chivo Wallet, which was the

00:20:00.640 --> 00:20:02.589
government issued wallet gifted to

00:20:02.590 --> 00:20:03.519
every citizen.

00:20:03.520 --> 00:20:05.409
Nobody could manage a 90

00:20:05.410 --> 00:20:06.729
day implementation like that

00:20:06.730 --> 00:20:07.689
properly. And so there was

00:20:07.690 --> 00:20:09.339
understandably technical missteps,

00:20:09.340 --> 00:20:10.479
and that was quite unfortunate

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:11.589
because, you know, the average

00:20:11.590 --> 00:20:13.149
person in El Salvador or anywhere

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:14.409
around the world doesn't really

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:15.489
understand Bitcoin.

00:20:15.490 --> 00:20:17.319
Salvadorans prefer to hold

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:18.339
and spend the U.S.

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:20.169
dollar, which, despite the recent

00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:22.269
spike in inflation, still has a much

00:20:22.270 --> 00:20:24.099
more stable value than Bitcoin.

00:20:24.100 --> 00:20:25.479
In terms of adopting Bitcoin as

00:20:25.480 --> 00:20:27.339
legal tender, what really matters

00:20:27.340 --> 00:20:29.229
is do we get bitcoin in

00:20:29.230 --> 00:20:30.369
the hands of people?

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:32.409
Do they use it as everyday money?

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:34.119
And that's what's going to make the

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:35.109
difference in terms of whether

00:20:35.110 --> 00:20:36.849
Bitcoin is widely used or not.

00:20:36.850 --> 00:20:38.469
So will Bitcoin ever become a

00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:40.089
commonly accepted medium of

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:40.959
exchange?

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:42.069
That's partly a bet that

00:20:42.070 --> 00:20:43.329
technologies like the Lightning

00:20:43.330 --> 00:20:44.949
Network will continue making it

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:46.809
easier and easier to use.

00:20:46.810 --> 00:20:48.339
And it's also a bet against the

00:20:48.340 --> 00:20:50.139
dollar as exploding U.S.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:52.059
debt puts increasing pressure on

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:53.889
the Federal Reserve to inflate the

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:54.669
money supply.

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:56.589
The only way that Bitcoin is going

00:20:56.590 --> 00:20:58.719
to move forward and get

00:20:58.720 --> 00:21:00.819
mass adoption is through bottom

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:02.229
up grassroots movements.

00:21:02.230 --> 00:21:03.549
Bitcoin has been eulogized

00:21:03.550 --> 00:21:05.229
repeatedly by journalists in the

00:21:05.230 --> 00:21:07.089
mainstream media, and yet it

00:21:07.090 --> 00:21:09.069
has always come back, surviving

00:21:09.070 --> 00:21:10.779
exchange collapses, bitter

00:21:10.780 --> 00:21:11.979
infighting and government

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:12.819
antagonism.

00:21:12.820 --> 00:21:14.619
The access to the payment system

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:16.599
should be something that is neutral,

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:17.799
apolitical.

00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:19.359
It should be a common resource,

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:20.259
right.

00:21:20.260 --> 00:21:22.269
And right now, barriers

00:21:22.270 --> 00:21:24.429
are being inserted into access

00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:26.259
to payments and banking, and

00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:27.759
it's becoming much more a question

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:30.099
of do you have political favor

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:30.969
as an industry.

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:31.869
And that's just not the way it

00:21:31.870 --> 00:21:33.349
should be in this country.

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:35.229
You know, there is a saying which is

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:36.699
Bitcoin is for enemies.

00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:38.859
This is really supposed to be a

00:21:38.860 --> 00:21:41.169
neutral technology and platform

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:43.359
where anyone who follows the rules

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:45.189
can use it regardless of if

00:21:45.190 --> 00:21:47.049
anyone else disagrees with who they

00:21:47.050 --> 00:21:48.279
are and what they're doing.

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:50.469
As the human drama unfolds,

00:21:50.470 --> 00:21:52.449
this decentralized, borderless,

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:54.279
censorship resistant software

00:21:54.280 --> 00:21:56.559
network continues to function

00:21:56.560 --> 00:21:58.180
just as Satoshi envisioned.

